ATP is a specification + docs repo (Markdown spec, README, examples, JSON Schemas, conformance shell scripts, Python check scripts) that also holds two packages, neither published to a package index: the Python ATP client in clients/python (clients/python/pyproject.toml), which pip builds with setuptools when it installs it (run: pip install ./clients/python), and the TypeScript ATP client in clients/typescript (clients/typescript/package.json), whose dev dependencies npm ci installs and which tsc builds (run: cd clients/typescript && npm ci && npm run build). The unit test suites are scripts/test_checks.py, the unit tests for the check scripts (run: python3 scripts/test_checks.py), clients/python/tests/test_atp_client.py, the unit tests for the Python client (run: cd clients/python && pip install . && python -m unittest discover -s tests), and clients/typescript/test/atp-client.test.ts, the unit tests for the TypeScript client (run: cd clients/typescript && npm ci && npm test); the conformance test suite (conformance/level1.sh, conformance/level2.sh) tests a running authority. There is no lint configuration, so no lint step applies.
